+    // The operand is an i1 carry value: 0 -> CLC, set -> SEC. A 'set' i1 can
+    // reach MC as -1 (sign-extended, the .td pattern's form) or as 1 (a plain
+    // i1 'true', e.g. the carry-in materialized for a 16-bit SBC), so treat any
+    // nonzero value as SEC rather than asserting a single encoding — the latter
+    // is an UNREACHABLE under asserts and silently mislowers under NDEBUG.
+    OutMI.setOpcode(MI->getOperand(1).getImm() == 0 ? MOS::CLC_Implied
+                                                    : MOS::SEC_Implied);
+    return;
